WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:33.730
The New Panda!

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:39.910
Internet

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:39.910
Comics & Games

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.700
Hey, Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.330
You've been doing that for a while,

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.830
but what exactly are you doing?

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.830
It's a side job.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.150
We just had our third child,

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.560
and our middle one is 
starting elementary school,

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.260
so she needs quite a few things.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.440
I see.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.640
If you're bored, would 
you help me out, Panda?

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.420
If it's solely for the purpose 
of relieving my boredom, sure.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.430
Apparently, "social etiquette"
doesn't exist in your dictionary.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.780
Then will you put these ads 
into these tissue packs?

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:16.260
Sure.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:48.520
This job doesn't just look dull. 
It actually is dull, isn't it?

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.030
Those pandas are doing a side job!

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.980
I guess the zoo's fallen 
on hard times, too.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.440
What?

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.870
Please stop at once!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.290
What zoo would allow their pandas 
to be seen doing side jobs?

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.010
I overheard a customer say that the zoo

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.120
must be going through some hard times.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.340
Come on.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.390
Visitors will flock in to see us 
doing something so unusual.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.600
We can't have them flock in for that.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.300
So it'd be okay if they 
couldn't see us, right?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.120
Huh?

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.180
We can do the side job 
if we aren't seen, right?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.970
All right, fine...

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.650
Hey, now.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.110
Why'd you okay their side job?

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.990
Well, it's okay if nobody 
sees them, isn't it?

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:42.860
It's not okay for pandas to 
sneak around doing side jobs.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.510
Please don't let the pandas trick you.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.120
Well, Mr. Full-time has a 
lot going on right now.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.620
Oh, come on. 
We need to be proper about this.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.630
Oh, that's right.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.040
I have a message from the zoo director.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.120
Starting next week, 
we'll have a temp panda.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.010
A temp panda?

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.320
Thanks for all your hard work!

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.360
What am I going to do, Panda?

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.030
What is it, Mr. Full-time Panda?

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.700
The arrival of a temp panda isn't good.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.120
Why's that?

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.630
There's no need for three 
pandas at this zoo.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.330
We might be laid off.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.500
Laid off?

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:43.470
Polar Bear's Café

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.430
Hey, Miss Sasako.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.390
What do you do on your days off?

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.390
On my days off? I take the day off.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.890
Yeah, but what do you do?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.990
I take all day off.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.880
That's not what I mean...

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.270
Never mind.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.820
What are you doing, Polar Bear?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.250
I'm making an octopus-shaped hot dog.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.430
An octopus-shaped hot dog? I see.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:15.480
What the heck is this?!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.920
An octopus-shaped hot dog.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.510
It's sort of scary.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.340
How'd you even make 
this out of hot dogs?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.550
It accents any lunch box.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.880
I don't think it would even 
fit in a lunch box...

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.610
What's going on with you? 
You seem happy.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:41.050
I might be laid off.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.360
Do you understand what that means?

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.440
Of course!

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:50.590
When Mr. Temp Panda 
comes, I might be laid off!

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.900
Wouldn't getting laid off be bad?

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.870
Not at all.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.330
Then I can boldly laze around at home.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.900
That's a rather new way 
to approach that.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.300
It must be a lot of fun being you.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:10.610
I hope Mr. Temp Panda 
gets here soon.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.600
This is...

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.770
Temp

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:20.250
Mr. Temp Panda, who'll 
be starting here today.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.450
I'm Temp Panda.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.020
Pleased to meet you.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.340
Nice to meet you.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.810
If you have any questions, 
feel free to ask these two.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:32.740
Yes, sir!

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:37.280
Also, we'll be getting some 
preschoolers this morning,

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.210
so make sure you give 
them plenty of service.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.590
Mr. Panda! Mr. Panda!

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.630
Mr. Panda!

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.960
Panda and Mr. Temp Panda,

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:54.440
I'm going to hide over 
there and work on this,

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.560
so I'll leave the morning to you.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.480
What on earth are you talking about?

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.160
How could you be doing a side job?

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.610
I'm just putting ads 
into tissue packs.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.150
That's not what I meant!

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.450
Is that something pandas 
should be doing?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.670
Talk to him, Panda.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.450
Okay, after I eat.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:25.890
Let's work harder to show the 
cuteness of pandas!

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:29.510
But if I just laze around, 
it's already cute.

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.360
Is that really enough for a panda?

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.430
Let's work harder on lazing around!

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.890
Work harder on lazing around?

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:47.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:54.120
I don't think that's the right 
kind of lazing around.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.610
True.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:58.740
Lazing around should be more like,

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.450
not the stern kind of lazing around,

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:04.790
but the lazing around 
kind of lazing around.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.880
I don't think this is something 
to state so passionately.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:11.300
Mr. Temp Panda 
sounds very serious.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.340
Of course, the relaxed kind 
of lazing around is cuter.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:19.770
But he's a pro at lazing, right?

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.730
So cute!

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.930
Mr. Panda!

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.920
Mr. Panda!

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.410
So cute!

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:41.750
That's why we're going to 
be holding an election.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.140
An election?

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.440
To decide who's going to 
be the central panda.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:52.360
We're going to have the visitors 
vote on the cutest panda.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:53.720
Choosing the central panda?

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.190
With only three of you?

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.470
I think we can leave 
that aspect alone...

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:06.440
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.320
Panda

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.320
Election

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.320
Everyone Please Vote!

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:12.480
Ballot 
Box

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.220
How's that look?

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.040
I think it looks good.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.830
What's that? An election?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:22.870
What's this?

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.870
I like that one.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.120
How about that panda?

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.120
The visitors seem to 
be interested, too.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.590
This could get exciting.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.310
I'm going to do my best!

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.520
For my wife and kids!

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.250
Service, service!

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.830
Wow!

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:43.830
Service!

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.680
So cute!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.770
Service, service!

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.480
That's not all...

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.940
I don't think I've ever seen 
him so backed into a corner.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.940
Service, service!

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.360
I think it's a good thing. 
He's trying real hard.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.250
Now!

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.710
Mr. Panda!

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.470
How cute.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:21.260
I see what he did there.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.540
What a pro.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.620
He's just laying there!

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.060
So cute!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.580
Hasn't changed at all.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.530
Just like the usual Panda...

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:39.390
I'm going to shamelessly laze around.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:42.300
That's what's so cute about me.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.090
I fell asleep...

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:07.020
And now, the results...

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:13.980
First place: Mr. Temp Panda.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.790
What?

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.290
Thank you!

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.450
Second place: Panda.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:24.910
What? Second place?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.330
Fourth place: Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.530
Why am I fourth?

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:31.910
Or rather, why was 
third place skipped?

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.190
Well...

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.170
1st: Temp Panda
300 votes

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:33.920
2nd: Panda 
200 votes

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:34.670
3rd: Handa 
3 votes

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:35.500
4th: Full-time Panda 
2 votes

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.960
I lost to Panda, who was sleeping...

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.720
Or rather...

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:46.330
I lost to Mr. Handa, who was cleaning.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.230
Oh. I-I'm sorry...

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.840
And so what happened to 
Mr. Temp Panda?

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:00.400
He's going to his next temp site.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.780
This was only short term.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.240
If it was so short term,

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:08.760
was there any reason to make
 this harsh ranking?

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:12.040
Cheer up, Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.190
This'll be on me.

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.470
Fourth place isn't so bad.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:18.920
At least it's not tenth place.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.380
I've lost my confidence as a panda...

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.740
Pardon me, but if you'd like,

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.810
I'll trade places with you 
at the Panda Corner.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:32.160
I do pretty well as a panda.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.770
Maybe I'll quit being a panda.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.770
Could I get a caramel 
latte, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:41.530
How about you take that off?

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.330
Okay.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:54.000
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:53.420
Reunion at the Grizzly Bar!

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.420
Hey, Wolf, how ya doin'?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:11.960
Tiger!

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:12.850
Hey!

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:20.700
Oh?

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.740
What?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.600
Looks like you gained some weight

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.010
in the short time I haven't seen you.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:30.510
Well, my wife makes some great food.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.050
Gained some weight from 
a happy marriage, eh?

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:34.240
And you call yourself a fierce beast?

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.420
Oh, shut up.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:37.830
Looks like you haven't changed.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.950
Yeah.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.760
Wolves don't look like 
wolves if we gain weight.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.760
Hey, it's been a while.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.780
What are you guys up to today?

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:50.770
Well, today we're getting together...

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.720
...with another old friend of ours.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:56.690
I see. Then your first 
drinks will be on me.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.430
Awesome! I'll take a martini.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.110
Could I get another bourbon?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.150
Sure.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.750
So Lion's gonna be late?

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:07.830
Apparently his flight's been delayed.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.570
Well, he always seems so busy.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:13.070
I heard you took over your family's 
Japanese confectionery shop.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:13.580
Yeah.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:20.190
Toraya

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.510
Must be nice,

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.400
being the rich son of a shop that's 
been in business for generations.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.210
<i>Welcome.</i>

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:26.380
Sweet
Paw

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:25.360
Our sweet paws that came out 
last year became a huge hit.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:31.300
Polar 
Bear 
Bun

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.890
Not to mention our Polar Bear Buns

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.510
and Black Bear Buns are popular as ever,

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:31.300
Black 
Bear 
Bun

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.180
so it's been really busy.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.780
Sweet paws, eh?

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.230
Who knew you had those kind of skills?

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:39.200
Not to mention we have another 
kid coming this year...

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.620
Whoa, really?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.060
How many's that?

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.580
Our sixth.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.440
They're super cute. Wanna see?

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.080
You're supposed to be a fierce beast.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.810
Stop showing me pictures of your kids.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:50.200
Isn't she cute?

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.660
This is our oldest at her 
 Shichi-go-san celebration.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:55.870
You're totally like a 
stay-at-home dad now.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.870
Well, I'm at that age.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:01.830
You're a fierce beast. 
Stop settling down so much.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.880
What about you, Wolf?

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.260
We don't need to talk about me.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:09.780
Are you still working at that bakery?

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:10.910
Well, yeah.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:14.580
Don't you have to look kind 
to work at a bakery?

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.220
Is that really a job for a fierce beast?

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.670
Well, you're working at a 
traditional confectionery shop.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.900
You've got a point.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.370
There you go.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:30.650
Cheers!

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:35.170
You know...

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:37.120
Have you thought about 
becoming independent?

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.330
Well, yeah.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.980
But before that...

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.190
I'd like to relax for a year
 on some southern island,

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:49.050
howling as the tropical wind blows by.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.490
I want to find something 
I really want to do.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.110
What the heck?

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:58.290
You're still trying to find yourself?

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.970
Well, I don't want to work 
at a bakery forever.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:05.100
Wolf, stop trying to find yourself.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.740
You're not supposed to find yourself,

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.200
you're supposed to choose yourself.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.360
Yeah, he's right! Exactly right!

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.900
Your next job should be
 opening your own bakery!

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:18.990
Become a lone wolf.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.750
Just so you know,

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.000
wolves are animals that 
are usually in packs...

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.370
Sorry.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.670
Hey! Sorry I'm late!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:32.170
Hey, Lion! It's been a while!

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:34.440
I was on a business trip in New York,

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.580
and I was delayed on a 
domestic flight layover.

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:40.080
What the heck? How cool is that?

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.020
Nothing less from a 
trading company man.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.850
Well, first, let's 
toast to our reunion.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:48.170
Cheers!

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:54.740
It's been a while since I 
was at the Grizzly Bar.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:59.640
It's really nostalgic, even though 
it hasn't been <i>that</i> long.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:02.810
I just recently saw Impala.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.710
Oh, what's he up to?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.260
He's at some agency,
pushing himself way too hard.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:11.200
He was so timid before.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:14.680
Looks like you've been keeping busy.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.970
Yeah, at this place.

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:20.140
Wow, you're exchanging business cards?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.220
It's pretty great working 
at a major corporation.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:27.080
It's a large-scale company, and I get 
a satisfaction I can't experience locally.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:31.550
Trying to keep up with 
the breakneck pace of the city

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:35.940
is tough, even for a hunter like me.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:41.330
"Even for a hunter like me"?

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:42.790
What?

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:47.080
"Even for a hunter like me"?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.130
W-What the hell?

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:52.690
Your mom always caught 
your food for you.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:55.000
You've totally changed, Lion.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.390
Hey, I just wanted to see 
how it felt to say that.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.570
We were totally into 
hip hop, weren't we?

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:09.580
Quite a bit.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:12.270
Haven't been listening 
to hip hop lately.

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.120
Pardon the intrusion.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.630
It's a bit too hardcore now.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:36.380
I've been going for more 
of an ambient sound.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.510
I've only been listening to children's 
songs since I have kids.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.250
We used to go to concerts 
all the time.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.120
Especially MC 469MA.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:46.910
The mysterious, elusive rapper.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:50.000
He gave me chills. 
He was so charismatic.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.680
Just thinking about him gives me
goosebumps, even though I'm a tiger.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:55.360
I got goosebumps, too.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.060
Yeah.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:00.320
But it's been a while, 
so he's a person of the past.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.780
What?!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.080
Are you dissin' 469MA?!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.560
No, that's not what I meant.

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.990
But he disappeared suddenly, 
without a trace.

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.710
But that's exactly why he 
lives on in our hearts

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.530
as the legendary rapper.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:19.250
I never thought I'd hear Lion say that.

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:22.450
You were even copying his style.

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:24.720
Well, animals change.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:27.400
Man, what the hell?

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.380
That's our youth...

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.060
How lame.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:37.210
Hey, where should we go next?

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:40.340
Sorry, I should probably get going.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.510
I have brunch with a client tomorrow.

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:44.330
Really? Are you serious?

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:48.290
Lions shouldn't be 
talking about brunch!

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:00.130
What the hell?!

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:10.810
Whoa, MC 469MA!

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:14.230
<i>Hey, man!</i>

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:19.150
<i>The name's 469MA, the biggest, baddest predator to roam the land</i>

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:20.450
<i>My ultimate weapons</i>

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.180
<i>Are these black claws on my hand</i>

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:25.620
<i>You better thank god that
I don't use these, son</i>

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.170
<i>The Earth's heating up from my scene</i>

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:31.000
<i>Shredding global warming with my rhyme</i>

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.290
<i>4, 6, 9, MA.</i>

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.500
4, 6, 9, MA!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:39.050
<i>4, 6, 9, MA!</i>

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:40.420
<i>Grizzly!</i>

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:47.210
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:49.380
<i>The ice is melting up in my lair</i>

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:50.900
<i>Everybody's in despair</i>

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.280
<i>This biggest carnivore</i>

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:55.350
<i>Soon won't be here anymore</i>

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:57.560
<i>Live on!</i>

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:58.460
<i>Live on!</i>

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.760
<i>Live on!</i>

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:02.320
<i>For having lived this long, 
I give props to the seals</i>

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.630
<i>Word! Props to the seals</i>

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.610
Those rhymes give me chills!

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:07.910
Those lyrics bring tears to my eyes!

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:09.980
Thank ya, man.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.400
Wow...

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:16.970
So cool.

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:21.100
I have mad respect for 
MC 469MA after all.

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:22.140
Me, too!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.090
Same here!

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.240
I respect him more!

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:30.560
Our youth is forever.

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:32.390
Yeah!

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:35.480
Fo' sho'.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.330
Let's go to karaoke.

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:47.550
What about your brunch tomorrow?

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:48.870
It's all good.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.820
All right. Let's go till morning.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:53.440
You better not howl into the mic.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:54.710
Sing.

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:57.030
Hey, I want to make a 
reservation for three beasts.

00:21:57.030 --> 00:21:58.500
Got a room?

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:11.420
A gift from 469MA, 
in honor of their reunion.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:23:59.990
Next Time

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.850
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:01.080
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:04.630
Let's say 500 good things 
about you, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:06.040
Go for it, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.090
I'm supposed to say them myself?

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:09.880
Could we cancel this plan?

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:10.590
Oh.

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:11.970
What is it, Polar Bear.

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:13.960
Nothing. Please continue.

00:24:14.470 --> 00:24:15.390
Continue.

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:17.180
Are you okay, Polar Bear?

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:18.390
Let's end this.

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.680
Next week, on Polar Bear's 
Antiques Roadshow—

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.840
Polar Bear's Café! Are you okay?!

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:24.000
Animal Field Baseball 
What's Jacu Coffee!?

00:24:22.840 --> 00:24:24.000
Enjoy!
